From: serlk <22211586+Serlk@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wolfssljni: session cache without freed sessions and races

external/wolfssljni is the wolfSSL JNI/JSSE provider (Copyright (C) wolfSSL
Inc., GPL-2.0-or-later); this changes three of its files under the same
licence.

SSLSessionContext.setSessionTimeout() threw
"IllegalStateException: Object has been freed" as soon as the session
cache held a session whose connection had been closed: the cache keeps
such sessions for resumption, their WOLFSSL object is freed with the
connection, and updateTimeouts() called into that object for every entry.
An application that sets the timeout per connection (in its hostname
verifier, for one) failed on every connection after the first closed one.
The cache table itself, a LinkedHashMap, was read and written by all
connection threads without any lock.

- WolfSSLAuthStore: every access to the session table holds one lock
  (lookup and resume, insert, the id listings, the timeout walk, resize).
  The timeout walk removes timed-out and invalidated sessions from the
  table and does not touch their native session; a lookup that finds an
  invalidated entry removes it, so the peer's next good session can be
  stored. resizeCache() copied the empty new table into the old one and
  lost every session; it keeps them now.
- WolfSSLImplementSSLSession: a session without a live WOLFSSL object
  keeps a timeout it is given and applies it when it is attached to a
  connection again (resume). getId() returns the id the session had
  instead of printing a stack trace and returning null once the
  connection is gone.
- WolfSSLSession: setSessTimeout()/getSessTimeout() are synchronized like
  freeSSL(), so the object cannot be freed between the check and the
  native call; setSessTimeoutIfActive() reports a freed object through its
  return value for callers that share the object with other threads.
---
  external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/WolfSSLSession.java    |  47 ++++++++++-
  .../src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLAuthStore.java    | 118 +++++++++++++++++++---------
  .../com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLImplementSSLSession.java   |  42 ++++++++--
  3 files changed, 161 insertions(+), 46 deletions(-)

diff --git a/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/WolfSSLSession.java b/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/WolfSSLSession.java
index a0d38a7..1ffcc5a 100644
--- a/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/WolfSSLSession.java
+++ b/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/WolfSSLSession.java
@@ -1050,10 +1050,13 @@ public class WolfSSLSession {
      * @see         #setSession(long)
      * @see         #getSession(long)
      */
-    public long setSessTimeout(long t) throws IllegalStateException {
+    public synchronized long setSessTimeout(long t)
+        throws IllegalStateException {
 
         long session;
 
+        /* synchronized like freeSSL(): the native object cannot be freed
+         * between this check and the native calls below */
         if (this.active == false)
             throw new IllegalStateException("Object has been freed");
 
@@ -1075,7 +1078,7 @@ public class WolfSSLSession {
      * @see         #setSession(long)
      * @see         #getSession(long)
      */
-    public long getSessTimeout() throws IllegalStateException {
+    public synchronized long getSessTimeout() throws IllegalStateException {
 
         if (this.active == false)
             throw new IllegalStateException("Object has been freed");
@@ -1083,6 +1086,46 @@ public class WolfSSLSession {
         return getSessTimeout(this.getSession());
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Sets the timeout in seconds in the WOLFSSL_SESSION of this object,
+     * if this object has not been freed.
+     * <p>
+     * For callers that hold a reference to an object another thread may
+     * free at any time (a session cache walking its entries): the check
+     * and the native call are one step with respect to
+     * <code>freeSSL()</code>, and a freed object is reported through the
+     * return value.
+     *
+     * @param t time in seconds to set
+     * @return WolfSSL.SSL_SUCCESS on success,
+     *         WolfSSL.JNI_SESSION_UNAVAILABLE if this object has been freed
+     *         or its session is unavailable, or negative values on failure.
+     */
+    public synchronized long setSessTimeoutIfActive(long t) {
+
+        long session;
+
+        if (this.active == false)
+            return WolfSSL.JNI_SESSION_UNAVAILABLE;
+
+        session = getSession(getSessionPtr());
+        if (session == 0)
+            return WolfSSL.JNI_SESSION_UNAVAILABLE;
+
+        return setSessTimeout(session, t);
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * Tells if the native object behind this one is still allocated.
+     * The answer can be outdated as soon as it is returned, unless the
+     * caller keeps other threads from calling <code>freeSSL()</code>.
+     *
+     * @return true if <code>freeSSL()</code> has not been called
+     */
+    public synchronized boolean isActive() {
+        return this.active;
+    }
+
     /**
      * Sets the timeout in seconds in the given SSL object.
      *
diff --git a/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLAuthStore.java b/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLAuthStore.java
index 57538b8..644ed62 100644
--- a/external/wolfssljni/src/java/com/wolfssl/provider/jsse/WolfSSLAuthStore.java
